    rdfs:label "Evidence for Lignum Quassia used in Brewing, Malting & Distilling: J. R. McCulloch, Dictionary of Commerce and Commercial Navigation (1880), scan p. 1266"@en ;
    <ontology/quoteText/#resource> "QUASSIA: (Ger. quassienholz; Fr. bois de quassie; Span. leño de casia). A beautiful tall tree (Quassia amara), growing in North and South America, and the West Indies. The wood is dense, tough, of a pale yellow colour, and odoriferous. Taste intensely and purely bitter. (British Pharmacopœia, 1867.) It is pretty extensively employed in the materia medica; an..."@en ;
